prep time: 20 minutes
cook time: 25 minutes
created: 2026-05-19
updated: 2026-05-19
---

Wash, peel and dice @pears{500%g}.

Chop @walnuts{40%g} coarsely with a knife. Put them in a #frying pan{} with a few sprigs of @fresh thyme{} and toast them on low for a few minutes, turning them often. Set them aside.

In the same frying pan, melt @butter{40%g} then add the diced pear, some thyme, a pinch of @fine sea salt{}, and @black pepper{}(freshly ground). Sauté on low for ~{5%minutes}.

Turn up the heat and deglaze with @dry white wine{60%g}. When the alcohol has evaporated, turn off the heat and set aside.

In a dry saucepan, toast @Carnaroli rice{320%g} with a pinch of salt, stirring frequently.

When the grains feel warm to the touch and start to become translucent, add @vegetable broth{1%l}(hot) one ladle at a time. Always let the rice absorb the broth before adding more.

= Mantecatura

When the risotto is ready, turn off the heat. Add @spicy gorgonzola{100%g}(cubed), @butter{40%g}(cold, cubed), and @Parmigiano Reggiano{100%g}(grated) and stir well until the risotto is creamy.

Finally, fold the sautéed pears into the risotto.

Season with @black pepper{}(freshly ground) to taste and plate the dish. Garnish with the toasted walnuts.